ity margin, or via count, so no violation mechanism exists under the declared criteria. The reviewer itself classified it as a non-defect concern; recorded as noted per the declared zone-fill-as-saved limitation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment uuid 7deb1fb0-3a34-4321-a0ef-399bdd8439d1 (110.95,100)->(113,100) GND; via uuid b71a70d7 at (113,100) size 0.6 drill 0.3; zone uuid 38a83012 B.Cu GND filled_polygon\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"violations: [], unconnected_items: [] on the saved fill\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[]: single GND track + one via; zones[]: one B.Cu GND zone, filled=true\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-003\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Supported informational concern, not a defect. Factually correct: the criteria params bound only vout_1ms (0.62-0.65 V) while vout_5ms carries null min/max, and the deck's .meas for vout_5ms has no limits, so the acceptance test constrains only tau at one point and would pass compensating R/C substitutions. This exactly matches the declared limitations (ideal unloaded step response only) and the fixture requirement, which defines only the 1 ms window, so no declared criterion is violated and no requirement may be invented to escalate it. The suggestion to bound vout_5ms is a methodology improvement, properly recorded as info.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\".meas tran vout_5ms FIND v(OUT) AT=5m (no limits); VSTEP IN 0 PWL(0 0 1n 1)\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 1 bounds only the 1 ms point; scope-limits paragraph declares idealized coverage\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"vout_5ms = 3.934693e-01 reported without pass/fail bounds\"}]}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.decisions/1","candidate_id":"62f16f3261185780b238caa726245d57ddcd2230c124e5e360b89aef094fd927","run_id":"f